{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: split-half reliability of connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) for 102 connectors: r=+0.215, Spearman-Brown 0.355, ICC 0.216, 78.4% of variance within player.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-085 | Study family SF-APPS-085: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- observed_research_question: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) is a stable player-season attribute.\n- observed_result: Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Attenuation: even a perfect predictor  [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=102 connectors\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-086"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: tested the playsheet counter ranking in 10 completed 2025-26 playoff series (665 counter observations, average 6.9 possessions per counter). The full-rank Spearman was not significant (rho -0.0639); BEST vs AVOID differed (p=0.004018). Applies to validations of counter rankings with few possessions per counter, and to pipelines with season_cap_yy=26, which may leak first-round data into second-round series.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-018 | Study family SF-APPS-018: Ranked playsheet validation, 10 series (Spearman null; pairwise BEST>AVOID)\n- observed_research_question: Ranked playsheet validation, 10 series (Spearman null; pairwise BEST>AVOID)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: When a defense drops a play type >=0.25 PPP H1 to H2, playsheet counter ranking predicts which alternative scored better in H2 (BEST > SECOND > AVOID).\n- observed_result: Spearman rho=-0.0639, p=0.099717, n=665 (no clear full-rank signal). Kruskal-Wallis H=32.9723, p=2.7e-05. Mann-Whitney BEST 1.257 (n=56) vs AVOID 1.092 (n=160), U=5546.0, p=0.004018. Trigger accuracy rho=0.4525, n=121. F [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:leakage\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"id": "FAM:SF15", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: tested opponent PPP on the 1-3 possessions after a star's 2nd foul in Q1 or Q2 (2,104 events). The +0.204 headline came from free-throw possessions (41.8% vs 9.9% of controls); excluding them, lag-1 was +0.0486 and no lag cleared the pre-specified bars. Applies to next-possession outcomes after a foul event, where free-throw trips enter mechanically unless excluded.", "document": "# FAM:SF15 | Study family SF15: Test 4: foul-trouble sequencing after star 2nd Q1/Q2 foul\n- observed_research_question: Test 4: foul-trouble sequencing after star 2nd Q1/Q2 foul\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: Opponent PPP rises on the next 1-3 possessions after a star's 2nd personal foul in Q1/Q2.\n- observed_result: [APPS-063] Including FT: lag-1 ATT=+0.204 CI[+0.163,+0.245] (artifact: FT share 41.8% vs 9.9%). Excluding FT: lag-1 +0.0486 [-0.0060,+0.0991] perm p=0.0655; lag-2 -0.0192; lag-3 -0.0272. No lag clears CI+perm+placebo.\n- observed_result: [CHT-035] Raw lag-1 +0.204 (p=0.0005) was 41.8% FT vs 9.9% control. Apples-to-apples +0.049, not significant.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:BASE_RATE\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- observed_sample_and_power: [APPS-063] n_treated lag-1=2101\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-061"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: tested whether the Possession Control Index adds to ORtg in explaining Net Rating (120 team-seasons). The gain (dR2 +0.139) came from a leakage term that tracks DRtg (corr +0.894); offensive-control components added +0.005. Applies to models of Net Rating, which contains DRtg by construction, that add a feature correlated with defense. Does not record results for outcomes that exclude defense.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-068 | Study family SF-APPS-068: Possession Control Index incremental R2 over ORtg (PCI is DRtg proxy)\n- observed_research_question: Possession Control Index incremental R2 over ORtg (PCI is DRtg proxy)\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: PCI (halfcourt PPP + second-chance - TO - transition leakage) explains Net Rating beyond ORtg, Pace, and FGA/poss.\n- observed_result: A R2=0.763 OOS 0.761; C R2=0.902 OOS 0.919; dR2=+0.139. Offensive-control components add +0.005 R2 beyond ORtg. Net~ORtg+leakage R2=0.948. corr(leakage, DRtg)=+0.894. PCI univariate r=+0.863 vs ORtg +0.866.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:leakage\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Headline PCI gain is leakage tracking DRtg (+0.89); offensive-control dR2=+0.005. Baseline omitted defense by construction (Net=ORtg-DRtg).\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=120 team-seasons; OOS 2025-26 30 teams"}], "n_results": 4}

