  "estimand": "The Intraclass Correlation Coefficient (ICC) of a defense's adjusted opponent points per possession (PPP) change from H1 to H2, across games within a team-season, and potentially across seasons for the same team, after controlling for confounding factors.",
  "unit": "Team-season for reliability assessment; game for within-team effect measurement.",
  "sample": "All available team-seasons (up to 120) from NBA 2022-23 to 2025-26. Each team-season will comprise approximately 82 regular-season games, plus playoff games.",
  "power": "Not specified, but historical evidence suggests achieving useful power for reliability metrics might be very difficult. A preliminary power analysis would be required, assuming a minimum detectable ICC.",
  "controls": "Control for game state variables (score differential, time remaining, quarter, home/away), opponent strength, pace, substitution patterns, garbage time, and exclude free-throw possessions or adjust for their rate. Consider controlling for specific opponent offensive play types if the H2-H1 effect is hypothesized to be play-type specific. Possibly use a matched-game design or regression adjustment to account for baseline opponent strength.",
  "falsification": "If the estimated ICC is below a pre-specified threshold (e.g., 0.5 for moderate reliability), or if the within-team variance of the H2-H1 change is significantly larger than the between-team variance. Also, if the H2-H1 change metric is found to be highly susceptible to artifacts (e.g., disproportionate impact of specific events like fouls leading to free throws).",
  "multiplicity": "If multiple definitions of 'H2-H1 change' or multiple control sets are explored, apply appropriate corrections (e.g., Bonferroni, FDR) for multiple testing.",
  "decision_rule": "The research question is deemed 'testable' and 'supported' if the ICC for the defense's H2-H1 effect (after controls) exceeds a pre-specified threshold (e.g., ICC > 0.5) with statistical significance (p < 0.05). If ICC is below this threshold or not significant, the hypothesis is 'rejected' or 'untestable' due to low reliability. If identified artifacts fundamentally distort the measurement, the outcome is 'artifact'.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs; NBA 2025-26 regular season and playoffs (complete as of 2026-06-21)."
 }
}

